<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petróleos de Venezuela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1976</span> · Also known as PDVSA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petróleos de Venezuela, S.A. (PDVSA) is Venezuela's state oil company, created on 1 January 1976 when the government nationalised the oil industry. For years it ranked among the world's largest oil companies. After a strike by its managers and workers in 2002–2003, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-chavez">Hugo Chávez</a> dismissed about 18,000 employees and used the company to fund social programmes; under-investment and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a> later caused its output to collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petroleos-de-venezuela.jpg" alt="Petróleos de Venezuela" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilfredor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edificio_PDVSA_5_de_Julio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
